  "notes": "One 34-point comb polygon (handle, head, 4 tines, 3 through-slots) extruded 0.0025 m in Z, then a smoothstep lift of up to 0.0095 m applied to every vertex by x, so the head curves up and the tine tips land at z = 0.012 m while the handle stays flat on z = 0.  Slots are open from the tip back to the tine root: 2.4 mm wide at the root and 3.0 mm at the tip; tines taper 4.45 -> 4.0 mm; head 25 mm wide; each tine edge carries a midpoint at x = 0.062 so the polished tip owns real quads.  Detail: a 1.2 x 50 mm tool is subtracted 1.2 mm into the handle (stamped trough, metal_dark), and x > 0.060 takes the polished ceramic tine tips.  AABB 0.190 x 0.025 x 0.012 m, one closed shell.",
